Z||000002||Phaeton||05-14-2000||06:19 AM||||If the headlight doors work properly then it it becomes obvious when the lights are on and the elves do not have to be heard.<P>But I did save my blue box just in case I get too old and start forgetting my seatbelt!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-14-2000||09:33 AM||||Just pulled that annoying little POS blue dingy thingy out of the Grape Ape.  It decided to get a mind of its own.  I suppose I could have traced the problem (did we ever figure out why it does what it does??), but why bother.  My headlight motors work great so I'm not too concerned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-14-2000||12:19 PM||||I worked out a test method. I haven't had time to try it.<P>You need a terminal map of the thing. Drop the terminal block off it's bracket then you remove one signal line at a time from the terminal block until it stops acting up.<P>The only line I can find that sould make a tone with the car running is the line from the hand brake. If that line is pinched or something else on that line is grounding it, it could activate the chime.<P>That I can tell all the other signals should be deactivted with the car running.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-14-2000||02:55 PM||||Mr. Ogre--What's a terminal block and a signal line?  I just had the E-brake cables cut/removed from the Grape Ape (getting ready for a GA/Beretta upgrade).  Do you think this would make any difference?||||reg||1
